A||||10||creativeeffects||Looking to buy||||10
Z||000000||creativeeffects||10-08-1999||09:10 AM||||I am looking to buy a fiero tonight, but I am not sure what to look for when I see it. It is an 84, 4-cylinder, automatic with 67,000 original miles. I know it was in a fender bender and the bumber was replaced. They are asking 1650.00. Please respond||||reg||10
Z||000001||BOILERMAKER||10-08-1999||10:10 AM||||I personally won't even look at another 4cyl again in my life, but that is a personal preference.  I have a V6 GT and will never look back.<P>Some people love the 4cyls and love them.  That's fine because they can have all of the ones that I turn down.||||reg||1
Z||000002||creativeeffects||10-08-1999||10:27 AM||||Is there a reason you don't like the 4cyc that has to due with reliability or just the lack of power? This car might be for my wife and she just likes the way it looks. I just want it to be reliable for a year or two.||||reg||5
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||10-08-1999||11:08 AM||||I think as far as reliability is concerned, the L4 is a better choice than the V6. The V6 however is way much more fun to drive!||||reg||1
Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||10-08-1999||11:26 AM||||I don't like 4's because they aren't as fun.  I have, along with myself, a couple of other people that are able to work on the 6cyls without the help of an outrageous mechanic.  Sometimes that's all the reason you need to not buy another 4cyl.<P>As far as reliability, I have no doubt that they are reliable, but so is the 6 if you keep care of it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||10-09-1999||01:05 AM||||well i don't know about the 4 cylinder but like boilermaker i have an 86 gt and the v6 is fun, but the four for the wife could be fine, but the price alone scares me. look around you can find newer models for that price, i only paid 900 for mine and it's even a fastback.and what fun i'm havin! goodluck.||||reg||1
Z||000006||2M4 Dale||10-09-1999||02:16 PM||||I've owned a number of true performance cars like a 69 GTO Judge, 69 Ford 460 XL etc. I know what it means to go fast. I personally like my little 2m4 a lot. It's definatly no slouch and man will it go around corners. All this at 28+mpg. Don't be afraid to buy a four cly.||||reg||14
Z||000007||BOILERMAKER||10-11-1999||09:11 AM||||As far as gas mileage, I've gotten 30 before and consistantly in the high 20's.  The 30 came (believe it or not) in Tennessee going around 76mph with the air on.  I figured out the mileage and boy was I a happy camper.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||10-12-1999||12:43 AM||||I generally get around 25 mpg in my 4 banger, and in 3 270 mile round trips I've averaged 30 mpg each time, at an average speed of 70 mph.  It may be underpowered, but the Duke is a damn good engine.  I beat on mine, run it up nearly to the red line (around 4800 revs), had it over 95 mph on the highway, and cruised at 70+ mph for an hour and then some, and it hasn't blown up yet!  :^)  It amazes me.  Of course, I still want a V6...||||reg||14
Z||000009||DJRice||10-12-1999||09:11 AM||||Both cars are pretty fun to drive.  If you take the 4 cyl for a spin you will no doubt enjoy yourself, and you will probably buy the car.  <P>However, as soon as you get the opportunity to drive a V6, you will want a V6.  <P>And theres nothing wrong with that because the Fieros are like Lays Potato Chips.  "You cant have just one."<P>BTW, Even for the low milage, that price does seem kinda high.  My brother just bought an 86 SE V6 with the same amount of miles for $1200.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||87GT||10-12-1999||07:16 PM||||I always watch the Fiero auctions on ebay and I rarely see a 84 Fiero go over a $1000.  I think I saw one(84) go for about $1100 once and it was in perfect shape.  The reserve was met on it and somebody got a nice looking 84 fiero.  The price is way too high on the one your interested in.  Anyways, good luck on getting a fiero. 8-)||||reg||1
